{"agent":"impl-governor-core","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"If a governed load signal is absent from `load` while other governed signals are present, `_load_step` fails to treat the absent signal as unavailable. For example, with `params.load_thresholds` containing both `\"cpu\"` and `\"mem\"`, `last.load=Ladder(level=2, at=0.0)`, `now=400` (cooldown 300), and `load={\"cpu\": 0.0}` (`\"mem\"` missing), `seen` is `[\"cpu\"]`, `blind` is `False`, `cand` is `0`, and the function returns `Ladder(0, 400)`. The load ladder drops from level 2 to 0 even though the missing `\"mem\"` reading could still be high. This violates the requirement that unavailable readings hold the ladder and are never read as zero; `not seen` handles the all-absent case, but partial absence is not marked blind.","digest":"d1acd4ff510bf8a8","location":"ddflow/core/govern.py:_load_step","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/govern.py:_load_step"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":24267,"diff_sha":"394b2afa339595def1738cfa567c0757eb8799d1f7b0244936580da7dd84c448","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":865.7,"excluded_bytes":1385362,"excluded_files":22,"excluded_paths":["README.md","ddflow/config.py","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.context_mark_1.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.context_mark_2.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.context_mark_3.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.context_mark_4.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.cooldown_s.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.deep_floor.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.govern.effort_cap_1.toml","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.